WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.875 --> 00:00:05.044
♪ ♪

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

3
00:00:23.929 --> 00:00:26.398
♪ ♪

4
00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.105
<i>Previously on</i>
Star Trek: Strange New Worlds...

5
00:00:33.238 --> 00:00:35.741
I'm in a relationship.
My life is complicated.

6
00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:37.076
Because Carol is pregnant.

7
00:00:37.209 --> 00:00:39.579
LA'AN:
Maybe I could be someone

8
00:00:39.679 --> 00:00:41.180
who takes chances more often.

9
00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:43.015
Spock and I made it very clear
with each other.

10
00:00:43.082 --> 00:00:44.349
No complicated expectations.

11
00:00:44.416 --> 00:00:45.585
Just fun times.

12
00:00:45.718 --> 00:00:47.352
(growls)

13
00:00:47.453 --> 00:00:48.688
- (grunts)
- (whimpering)

14
00:00:48.754 --> 00:00:50.089
CHAPEL:
You punched a dinosaur?

15
00:00:50.222 --> 00:00:51.924
I broke my hand
and I don't feel any pain.

16
00:00:52.024 --> 00:00:53.793
My whole body
feels more attuned.

17
00:00:53.926 --> 00:00:55.961
- M'BENGA: And your mind?
- Confused.

18
00:00:56.061 --> 00:00:57.429
Being Vulcan
affected you differently.

19
00:00:57.563 --> 00:00:59.064
- You are aggressive.
- (screams)

20
00:00:59.164 --> 00:01:01.100
Are you going to try
and take over the galaxy now?

21
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:02.868
I don't know.

22
00:01:09.575 --> 00:01:11.777
(signal chiming)

23
00:01:23.956 --> 00:01:27.459
KIRK:
Personal log. Stardate 2903.9.

24
00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:29.361
The Future
Federation Leaders retreat

25
00:01:29.461 --> 00:01:31.396
was an overwhelming success.

26
00:01:31.463 --> 00:01:32.965
But my plan to hitch a ride home

27
00:01:33.098 --> 00:01:36.401
with fellow attendees
La'An and Spock has hit a snag.

28
00:01:36.502 --> 00:01:40.472
We detected a mysterious signal
in an uncharted region of space.

29
00:01:40.573 --> 00:01:43.475
It's the kind of thing
I joined Starfleet for.

30
00:01:43.576 --> 00:01:45.978
and yet for the first time.

31
00:01:46.111 --> 00:01:50.249
I can't shake the feeling
I'm in the wrong place.

32
00:01:51.584 --> 00:01:52.652
SPOCK:
Curious.

33
00:01:52.752 --> 00:01:54.019
The signal is being broadcast

34
00:01:54.119 --> 00:01:55.721
over an old
Federation frequency.

35
00:01:55.821 --> 00:01:58.357
Spock. no one likes
a back seat sensor reader.

36
00:01:58.457 --> 00:02:00.092
Apologies.

37
00:02:02.662 --> 00:02:04.429
(quietly):
Is everything all right?

38
00:02:04.530 --> 00:02:07.667
At the retreat.
you seemed distracted.

39
00:02:07.767 --> 00:02:09.034
I'm fine.

40
00:02:12.037 --> 00:02:13.706
Now that we're closer.
can you pinpoint a signal?

41
00:02:13.806 --> 00:02:15.107
LA'AN:
Sending coordinates.

42
00:02:15.174 --> 00:02:17.677
It's just behind
that larger asteroid there.

43
00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:29.789
LA'AN:
My God. Is that...

44
00:02:29.889 --> 00:02:31.490
The Griffin.

45
00:02:32.892 --> 00:02:35.327
After all these years.

46
00:02:36.195 --> 00:02:37.897
Please tell me that there's...

47
00:02:38.831 --> 00:02:42.267
Sensors show
no life signs aboard.

48
00:02:44.837 --> 00:02:46.238
300 souls on board

49
00:02:46.371 --> 00:02:48.207
when she went missing
nine years ago.

50
00:02:48.307 --> 00:02:50.109
Last known location
light-years from here.

51
00:02:50.209 --> 00:02:53.212
Captain Taggert sent a report
to Starbase 1. and then...

52
00:02:53.312 --> 00:02:54.947
And then. the Griffin vanished.

53
00:02:55.047 --> 00:02:56.481
The most obvious explanation
was the Griffin

54
00:02:56.582 --> 00:02:57.917
was in the wrong place
at the wrong time.

55
00:02:58.017 --> 00:02:59.218
stumbled on a Klingon
Bird-of-Prey.

56
00:02:59.318 --> 00:03:00.820
its destruction covered up.

57
00:03:00.886 --> 00:03:02.722
SPOCK: A logical theory based
on its last known position

58
00:03:02.822 --> 00:03:04.256
is that a stellar flare
hit the Griffin

59
00:03:04.389 --> 00:03:05.591
while it entered warp.

60
00:03:05.691 --> 00:03:07.092
scattering it
over many light-years.

61
00:03:07.226 --> 00:03:08.828
That and every other theory
that Starfleet had

62
00:03:08.894 --> 00:03:11.096
doesn't explain
what we're looking at here.

63
00:03:12.732 --> 00:03:14.466
So. what the hell
really happened?

64
00:03:16.168 --> 00:03:18.103
Only one way to find out.

65
00:03:19.304 --> 00:03:20.673
Two flashlights. Really?

66
00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:22.374
You know. as soon as I'm back
on Enterprise.

67
00:03:22.441 --> 00:03:24.409
I'm gonna make sure
to reprimand whoever conducted

68
00:03:24.509 --> 00:03:26.178
- the last inspection.
- (chuckles)

69
00:03:26.245 --> 00:03:27.913
Starting to see
why you and Spock are perfect

70
00:03:28.013 --> 00:03:29.281
for one another.

71
00:03:30.783 --> 00:03:31.917
Not to worry.

72
00:03:32.051 --> 00:03:35.420
I was a Boy Scout
before I was Starfleet.

73
00:03:39.158 --> 00:03:40.793
Be prepared. right?

74
00:03:43.929 --> 00:03:45.998
LA'AN:
Stowaway?

75
00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.935
Gift. For my son.

76
00:03:50.035 --> 00:03:52.204
I was supposed to visit
this weekend. but then I got

77
00:03:52.271 --> 00:03:53.939
the call for the retreat
and I. uh...

78
00:03:54.039 --> 00:03:55.775
Couldn't pass up a chance to
meet Admiral Smillie in person.

79
00:03:55.875 --> 00:03:58.878
I've been studying his maneuvers
my whole career.

80
00:03:59.645 --> 00:04:02.114
Well. I am sure
David will understand

81
00:04:02.214 --> 00:04:05.217
as soon as he meets
his new little friend.

82
00:04:09.321 --> 00:04:11.156
Our discovery and coordinates
have been sent to Enterprise

83
00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:13.092
via long-range
transmission package.

84
00:04:13.158 --> 00:04:15.327
All right. then.

85
00:04:19.598 --> 00:04:21.633
Let's boldly go.

86
00:04:31.711 --> 00:04:33.112
(signal chiming)

87
00:04:33.212 --> 00:04:35.314
LA'AN:
Why aren't we floating?

88
00:04:36.982 --> 00:04:39.985
SPOCK: There is no scientific reason
this ship should have gravity.

89
00:04:41.721 --> 00:04:43.155
And yet...

90
00:04:43.288 --> 00:04:44.489
KIRK:
Well.

91
00:04:44.623 --> 00:04:47.727
that's unnerving
with a side of unsettling.

92
00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.129
I don't understand.

93
00:04:50.195 --> 00:04:52.431
It's like everyone
took a coffee break.

94
00:04:52.497 --> 00:04:54.433
And never returned.

95
00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.103
(baby crying)

96
00:05:00.605 --> 00:05:01.707
KIRK:
Do you hear that?

97
00:05:01.841 --> 00:05:03.976
LA'AN:
I don't hear anything.

98
00:05:04.076 --> 00:05:05.878
No hum of a warp core.

99
00:05:06.011 --> 00:05:07.612
no buzzing from life support.
nothing.

100
00:05:07.679 --> 00:05:09.281
SPOCK:
Readings show no signs of radiation.

101
00:05:09.381 --> 00:05:13.018
virus. parasite or unusual
anomalies of any kind.

102
00:05:13.819 --> 00:05:15.721
For all intents and purposes.

103
00:05:15.821 --> 00:05:17.823
this ship is perfectly safe.

104
00:05:19.658 --> 00:05:21.026
Right.

105
00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:24.997
Show of hands for anyone
who feels safe on the Griffin?

106
00:05:25.064 --> 00:05:27.432
(signal chiming)

107
00:05:27.532 --> 00:05:31.136
This appears to be the source
of the signal we detected.

108
00:05:32.671 --> 00:05:34.706
What's powering it?

109
00:05:36.575 --> 00:05:38.410
That is unclear.

110
00:05:42.347 --> 00:05:44.049
What did you do?

111
00:05:44.149 --> 00:05:45.951
I did nothing.

112
00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:53.492
This computer's last system
check indicates that all

113
00:05:53.592 --> 00:05:55.761
of the ship's power
should have expired years ago.

114
00:05:55.861 --> 00:05:58.330
So. it was asleep
and now it's awake?

115
00:05:59.398 --> 00:06:01.166
In a manner of speaking.

116
00:06:01.233 --> 00:06:02.868
Life support is now on line.

117
00:06:02.968 --> 00:06:04.937
But we have only one hour
before remaining power

118
00:06:05.037 --> 00:06:06.238
is drained for good.

119
00:06:06.338 --> 00:06:08.841
60 minutes to figure out
what happened here.

120
00:06:08.941 --> 00:06:10.609
SPOCK:
Oxygen level is stable.

121
00:06:10.742 --> 00:06:12.744
We can remove our masks.

122
00:06:22.754 --> 00:06:25.925
♪ ♪

123
00:06:30.695 --> 00:06:32.764
No shuttlecraft.

124
00:06:32.898 --> 00:06:34.266
No escape pods.

125
00:06:34.366 --> 00:06:35.935
Is that how the crew evacuated?

126
00:06:36.068 --> 00:06:37.903
Possible.

127
00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:42.041
but there's no shuttle log
or reports of pods jettisoning.

128
00:06:42.107 --> 00:06:44.109
And there are no records
of unusual discoveries

129
00:06:44.209 --> 00:06:45.945
or experiments.

130
00:06:47.446 --> 00:06:49.248
There appears to be...

131
00:06:49.314 --> 00:06:51.783
No sign of anything wrong.

132
00:06:51.884 --> 00:06:53.152
So...

133
00:06:53.919 --> 00:06:55.454
...where did everyone go?

134
00:06:57.689 --> 00:07:01.326
SPOCK: Perhaps answers can only be
uncovered by Division 12.

135
00:07:01.460 --> 00:07:02.727
LA'AN:
Division 12?

136
00:07:02.794 --> 00:07:04.329
Starfleet analysts
that run around

137
00:07:04.429 --> 00:07:06.165
investigating
unexplained phenomena

138
00:07:06.265 --> 00:07:08.133
can have their turn
when we're done.

139
00:07:08.267 --> 00:07:09.301
(exhales)

140
00:07:09.401 --> 00:07:11.036
We still have time to...

141
00:07:15.507 --> 00:07:16.876
Hello?

142
00:07:17.742 --> 00:07:19.011
Hello?

143
00:07:19.111 --> 00:07:21.413
We're here to help.

144
00:07:26.986 --> 00:07:29.221
I've been waiting for you.

145
00:07:30.489 --> 00:07:32.424
Wait.

146
00:07:50.809 --> 00:07:53.012
♪

147
00:07:54.413 --> 00:07:56.181
<i>PIKE: Space.</i>

148
00:07:57.516 --> 00:07:59.551
The final frontier.

149
00:08:01.186 --> 00:08:04.957
These are the voyages
of the starship Enterprise.

150
00:08:07.092 --> 00:08:08.894
Its five-year mission:

151
00:08:08.994 --> 00:08:12.097
to explore strange new worlds...

152
00:08:14.233 --> 00:08:16.635
...to seek out new life

153
00:08:16.735 --> 00:08:19.238
and new civilizations...

154
00:08:20.239 --> 00:08:24.376
...to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

155
00:08:24.476 --> 00:08:27.212
♪ ♪

156
00:08:54.673 --> 00:08:56.841
♪ ♪

157
00:09:20.765 --> 00:09:22.968
♪ ♪

158
00:09:40.052 --> 00:09:42.054
(device buzzing)

159
00:09:50.062 --> 00:09:52.931
There are no life signs present.

160
00:09:52.998 --> 00:09:55.067
It is as if the survivor
not only vanished.

161
00:09:55.134 --> 00:09:57.069
but was never here at all.

162
00:09:57.169 --> 00:10:00.372
Not enough power for her
to have transported out of here.

163
00:10:00.472 --> 00:10:03.008
Maybe she transported
before power was lost.

164
00:10:03.142 --> 00:10:05.110
I saw something like that
on the MLK.

165
00:10:05.177 --> 00:10:07.012
A landing party got caught
in the buffer.

166
00:10:07.146 --> 00:10:08.580
Engineering never got them out.

167
00:10:08.647 --> 00:10:10.182
An excellent theory.

168
00:10:10.282 --> 00:10:12.451
But readings show no signs
of any transmitted material.

169
00:10:12.551 --> 00:10:17.322
However. there are faint traces
of negatively charged ions.

170
00:10:17.422 --> 00:10:18.523
You mean a ghost?

171
00:10:18.657 --> 00:10:20.525
I mean negatively charged ions.

172
00:10:20.625 --> 00:10:22.794
The survivor we encountered
shed ions directly

173
00:10:22.894 --> 00:10:24.629
into this dead end.

174
00:10:24.696 --> 00:10:26.765
And then what?

175
00:10:26.831 --> 00:10:28.200
Drifted into space?

176
00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.202
This is where her trail ends.

177
00:10:30.302 --> 00:10:32.071
Let's find out where it began.

178
00:10:43.382 --> 00:10:45.050
LA'AN:
What could cause someone

179
00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:48.187
to emit negatively charged ions?

180
00:10:48.287 --> 00:10:50.889
This ship presents
many scientific contradictions.

181
00:10:51.022 --> 00:10:54.593
I would need more evidence
before positing a cogent theory.

182
00:10:55.660 --> 00:10:58.130
Evidence like that?

183
00:11:06.105 --> 00:11:09.241
The survivor's trail began on
the other side of these doors.

184
00:11:10.709 --> 00:11:13.078
Those markings...
they're from phasers.

185
00:11:13.178 --> 00:11:15.480
These are Starfleet.

186
00:11:16.381 --> 00:11:18.883
And those are Klingon.

187
00:11:18.983 --> 00:11:21.120
And these Vulcan.

188
00:11:24.189 --> 00:11:26.391
I am beginning to suspect
we are not the first party

189
00:11:26.491 --> 00:11:28.427
to board the Griffin.

190
00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:30.762
One party tried
to seal someone in.

191
00:11:30.895 --> 00:11:32.631
another tried to blast them out.

192
00:11:32.731 --> 00:11:34.866
So what's behind those doors?

193
00:11:34.933 --> 00:11:36.435
Watch our six.

194
00:11:36.568 --> 00:11:38.637
Spock. help me with the door.

195
00:11:41.506 --> 00:11:43.642
(soft clattering)

196
00:11:45.944 --> 00:11:48.213
(clattering continues)

197
00:11:49.448 --> 00:11:52.651
(baby crying)

198
00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.357
(baby crying)

199
00:12:18.143 --> 00:12:19.778
James?

200
00:12:19.878 --> 00:12:21.646
You all right?

201
00:12:23.248 --> 00:12:25.750
Sorry.
Thought I heard something.

202
00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.752
but it was nothing.

203
00:12:29.388 --> 00:12:32.457
Right. Well.
we've loosened the barricades.

204
00:12:41.233 --> 00:12:43.402
(doors squeaking)

205
00:13:01.953 --> 00:13:05.089
LA'AN: Empty body bags.
Where did the bodies go?

206
00:13:05.156 --> 00:13:06.825
The medical transporter
is offline.

207
00:13:06.925 --> 00:13:08.427
I can reroute power
and check the records.

208
00:13:08.527 --> 00:13:09.861
but it will take time.

209
00:13:09.961 --> 00:13:11.996
Which we're running out of.
Let's split up.

210
00:13:12.130 --> 00:13:13.598
Spock. get those records.

211
00:13:13.698 --> 00:13:15.099
We'll head to the bridge
to see what we can find out

212
00:13:15.166 --> 00:13:16.601
about the survivor
and where she might be.

213
00:13:16.668 --> 00:13:18.670
Meet back here in 20 minutes.

214
00:13:23.975 --> 00:13:26.345
- Stay safe. okay?
- Likewise.

215
00:13:50.535 --> 00:13:52.704
♪ ♪

216
00:13:57.642 --> 00:14:00.078
You don't really believe
in ghosts. do you?

217
00:14:00.178 --> 00:14:03.782
(scoffs)
No. but I'd love to give closure

218
00:14:03.882 --> 00:14:06.084
to the families
of the Griffin's crew.

219
00:14:06.217 --> 00:14:08.219
You're thinking
of Carol and David?

220
00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.589
What's David like?

221
00:14:10.722 --> 00:14:11.890
Hilarious.

222
00:14:12.023 --> 00:14:13.625
- Yeah?
- Beautiful. Happy.

223
00:14:13.725 --> 00:14:15.860
Takes after his mother
on all three.

224
00:14:15.960 --> 00:14:18.897
- And how is Carol?
- Oh. Carol's great.

225
00:14:18.997 --> 00:14:22.066
Incredible mom. Just got
approved for a dream project.

226
00:14:22.166 --> 00:14:25.003
Carol and I?

227
00:14:25.069 --> 00:14:26.805
Well...

228
00:14:28.873 --> 00:14:30.141
It's my fault really.

229
00:14:30.241 --> 00:14:32.611
She was never a fan
of Starfleet.

230
00:14:32.744 --> 00:14:36.681
Always worried I would die alone
somewhere in unknown space.

231
00:14:37.649 --> 00:14:41.052
No idea what would give her
that impression.

232
00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:43.522
Ah.

233
00:14:43.588 --> 00:14:47.392
I don't know how Sam balances
Starfleet and family.

234
00:14:47.459 --> 00:14:50.429
Well. I don't really
have that problem.

235
00:14:50.562 --> 00:14:53.064
Starfleet is my family.

236
00:14:56.935 --> 00:14:59.604
La'An. can I ask you something?

237
00:14:59.738 --> 00:15:01.640
Mm-hmm.

238
00:15:06.778 --> 00:15:08.713
No negatively charged ions.

239
00:15:09.781 --> 00:15:14.285
There's nothing
in this corridor but us.

240
00:15:15.086 --> 00:15:16.855
What were you going to ask me?

241
00:15:19.791 --> 00:15:21.726
Do you believe in ghosts?

242
00:15:21.826 --> 00:15:23.027
(scoffs)

243
00:15:23.127 --> 00:15:25.930
- (Kirk chuckles)
- Not funny.

244
00:15:33.705 --> 00:15:37.108
To confirm. the Griffin was not
boarded by an alien intruder.

245
00:15:37.175 --> 00:15:40.278
struck by a viral infection
or any unknown cosmic anomaly.

246
00:15:40.379 --> 00:15:42.013
COMPUTER:
Affirmative.

247
00:15:42.146 --> 00:15:44.048
Then why were the bodies
removed from the Griffin?

248
00:15:44.148 --> 00:15:46.418
What did Captain Taggert specify
in his orders?

249
00:15:46.485 --> 00:15:48.953
(glitching):
All bodies were transported

250
00:15:49.020 --> 00:15:51.690
by Chief Security Officer
Rose Harper.

251
00:15:51.823 --> 00:15:53.992
including the body
of the captain.

252
00:15:54.092 --> 00:15:57.261
Computer. tell me everything
on record about Harper.

253
00:15:58.096 --> 00:15:59.731
LA'AN:
Graduated top of her class.

254
00:15:59.831 --> 00:16:01.866
Rose Harper was known
to be detail-oriented.

255
00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.502
driven and ambitious.

256
00:16:03.635 --> 00:16:06.037
Sound like anyone you know?

257
00:16:07.772 --> 00:16:09.841
LA'AN:
Before the Griffin disappeared.

258
00:16:09.941 --> 00:16:12.043
Harper filed numerous
security reports

259
00:16:12.143 --> 00:16:15.447
about "erratic behavior"
spreading among the crew.

260
00:16:15.514 --> 00:16:16.848
Erratic?

261
00:16:16.948 --> 00:16:18.817
Violent outbursts.

262
00:16:18.917 --> 00:16:20.218
Self-harm. delusions.

263
00:16:20.351 --> 00:16:22.921
She reported each
to her superiors and medical.

264
00:16:23.021 --> 00:16:24.489
Everyone was thoroughly examined

265
00:16:24.589 --> 00:16:26.357
but medically cleared for duty.

266
00:16:27.158 --> 00:16:29.327
So. was she imagining
these incidents?

267
00:16:29.394 --> 00:16:31.362
Well. she certainly
didn't believe so.

268
00:16:31.463 --> 00:16:33.231
She added the doctor
to her list.

269
00:16:33.364 --> 00:16:34.866
And then the captain
after she believed

270
00:16:34.966 --> 00:16:36.401
he was blocking her reports
to Starfleet.

271
00:16:36.501 --> 00:16:38.369
As the cases spread ship-wide.

272
00:16:38.503 --> 00:16:41.005
Harper took radical steps.

273
00:16:41.105 --> 00:16:43.575
How radical?

274
00:16:50.749 --> 00:16:52.250
SPOCK:
How did they all die?

275
00:16:52.383 --> 00:16:54.285
13 strangulations.

276
00:16:54.385 --> 00:16:56.555
Eight stabbings.

277
00:16:56.655 --> 00:16:59.924
287 were transported
into open space

278
00:17:00.058 --> 00:17:02.594
while they were still alive.

279
00:17:04.395 --> 00:17:06.264
- (comms chime)
- La'An. this is Spock.

280
00:17:06.364 --> 00:17:08.199
I have uncovered troubling
information about the survivor

281
00:17:08.299 --> 00:17:10.635
we encountered
and recommend immediate...

282
00:17:15.474 --> 00:17:17.809
Computer. open doors.

283
00:17:19.377 --> 00:17:21.412
Computer.

284
00:17:22.246 --> 00:17:25.116
- (comms chime)
- I need assistance in sickbay.

285
00:17:27.786 --> 00:17:29.921
La'An?

286
00:17:31.623 --> 00:17:33.792
Jim. do you copy?

287
00:17:34.626 --> 00:17:36.795
(faint whoosh)

288
00:18:03.387 --> 00:18:04.789
HARPER:
Harper's personal log.

289
00:18:04.889 --> 00:18:07.291
Stardate... I don't know.

290
00:18:07.425 --> 00:18:09.728
The days are beginning
to bleed together.

291
00:18:09.794 --> 00:18:13.598
Captain Taggert and Dr. G'har
relieved me of duty.

292
00:18:13.665 --> 00:18:15.333
Confined me to quarters.

293
00:18:15.466 --> 00:18:16.768
No one believes me.

294
00:18:16.835 --> 00:18:19.771
But something is wrong
with this ship.

295
00:18:19.871 --> 00:18:22.340
Something is taking over
the crew.

296
00:18:26.077 --> 00:18:28.412
No transportation residue.

297
00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:31.850
And yet...

298
00:18:44.328 --> 00:18:47.498
(tricorder trilling)

299
00:19:13.725 --> 00:19:16.127
WOMAN:
Spock?

300
00:19:19.363 --> 00:19:21.733
(video glitching):
I need you to hear me.

301
00:19:21.833 --> 00:19:24.202
I need you to believe me.

302
00:19:26.905 --> 00:19:30.909
You can't trust any of them.
La'An.

303
00:19:36.014 --> 00:19:37.749
James.

304
00:19:37.882 --> 00:19:39.818
James. we need
to get off this ship now.

305
00:19:39.884 --> 00:19:41.820
Yeah.

306
00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:44.589
About that.

307
00:19:44.723 --> 00:19:47.158
Oh. my God.

308
00:19:49.894 --> 00:19:52.130
That's our shuttle.

309
00:20:06.010 --> 00:20:08.279
(gasps)
It is cold.

310
00:20:09.814 --> 00:20:13.517
I was counseling a patient.
There was a light.

311
00:20:13.652 --> 00:20:16.120
Then darkness.

312
00:20:16.220 --> 00:20:18.422
Then I could not breathe.

313
00:20:19.190 --> 00:20:21.760
Then I was in this bag.

314
00:20:21.826 --> 00:20:24.162
I do not understand what is...

315
00:20:25.529 --> 00:20:27.866
This... this is a dream.

316
00:20:27.966 --> 00:20:30.534
- Fascinating.
- I am having a nightmare.

317
00:20:30.669 --> 00:20:33.471
Why is Spock in my nightmare?

318
00:20:33.537 --> 00:20:35.707
These readings indicate
a living. breathing Vulcan.

319
00:20:35.807 --> 00:20:38.542
I will wake up and be safe.

320
00:20:38.643 --> 00:20:40.679
Perhaps it is a psychic
projection of some kind.

321
00:20:40.779 --> 00:20:42.580
Which puts the reliability
of my observations

322
00:20:42.681 --> 00:20:44.949
and faculties
in considerable doubt.

323
00:20:51.222 --> 00:20:53.091
This is deeply unsettling.

324
00:20:53.858 --> 00:20:55.593
On that. we are in agreement.

325
00:20:56.460 --> 00:20:57.929
What is happening?

326
00:20:58.029 --> 00:20:59.563
I do not know for certain.

327
00:20:59.664 --> 00:21:01.733
My current theory is
that an unknown phenomenon

328
00:21:01.866 --> 00:21:04.068
with a psychotropic area
of effect is causing anyone

329
00:21:04.202 --> 00:21:05.837
- who boards the Griffin to...
- The Griffin?

330
00:21:05.937 --> 00:21:08.639
Why am I on a missing
Federation ship?

331
00:21:08.740 --> 00:21:10.474
You are not.

332
00:21:10.541 --> 00:21:14.478
Spock. I am not an illusion.

333
00:21:14.545 --> 00:21:16.580
Then what are you?

334
00:21:20.518 --> 00:21:22.821
No sign of any ship in the area.

335
00:21:22.887 --> 00:21:24.723
So what blew up our shuttle?

336
00:21:24.856 --> 00:21:26.691
Here's what I know.
Spock was right.

337
00:21:26.791 --> 00:21:29.728
The Griffin is
Division 12's problem to solve.

338
00:21:30.528 --> 00:21:32.731
We only have 20 minutes
of life support left. James.

339
00:21:32.831 --> 00:21:34.398
Don't forget
the Griffin's escape pods

340
00:21:34.532 --> 00:21:36.567
and shuttles are gone.
and we also have a psychopath

341
00:21:36.667 --> 00:21:38.436
who can walk through walls
on board.

342
00:21:38.569 --> 00:21:40.371
LA'AN: We can't just sit around
and wait

343
00:21:40.471 --> 00:21:42.974
for the long-range message
Spock sent to reach Enterprise.

344
00:21:46.444 --> 00:21:49.180
If we can get more power
to comms up here.

345
00:21:49.247 --> 00:21:52.050
I think I can get an SOS signal
to anyone in the neighborhood.

346
00:21:52.116 --> 00:21:54.352
Yes. all right. okay. I'll have
Spock meet me in engineering.

347
00:21:54.418 --> 00:21:56.454
and we'll reroute power
and life support to the bridge.

348
00:21:56.587 --> 00:21:58.422
You think
that'll buy us enough time?

349
00:22:01.225 --> 00:22:03.294
- (comms chime)
- Spock. it's La'An.

350
00:22:03.394 --> 00:22:05.997
I need you
to meet me in engineering.

351
00:22:07.766 --> 00:22:09.633
Why me?

352
00:22:09.768 --> 00:22:13.071
Your theory is that I am
a hallucination. correct?

353
00:22:13.171 --> 00:22:17.108
If that is true. then why did
whatever looked into your mind

354
00:22:17.208 --> 00:22:18.810
choose me to conjure?

355
00:22:18.910 --> 00:22:21.846
I only know
that you are not T'Pring.

356
00:22:23.782 --> 00:22:28.052
When I was on my kahs-wan.
I was injured while hiking.

357
00:22:28.152 --> 00:22:30.654
Wildlife circled me.
waiting to strike.

358
00:22:30.789 --> 00:22:33.925
Trapped.
I experienced what humans

359
00:22:34.025 --> 00:22:36.961
refer to as a... panic attack.

360
00:22:37.061 --> 00:22:39.497
I centered my mind
by meditating.

361
00:22:39.597 --> 00:22:43.134
chanting a favorite couplet
by the great poet Ka'nina.

362
00:22:43.234 --> 00:22:46.570
(speaks Vulcan)

363
00:22:46.670 --> 00:22:47.872
"It will guide you home."

364
00:22:47.972 --> 00:22:51.342
It brought me back.
and I survived.

365
00:22:52.777 --> 00:22:54.078
You are the only person

366
00:22:54.145 --> 00:22:56.580
I have ever shared
that story with. Spock.

367
00:22:56.680 --> 00:22:59.150
Correct. And since
you are a product of my mind.

368
00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:02.353
you are able to recite the real
T'Pring's anecdote back to me.

369
00:23:04.856 --> 00:23:09.193
Well. one thing we can
both agree on is a shared desire

370
00:23:09.293 --> 00:23:11.695
to disembark this ship
immediately.

371
00:23:12.797 --> 00:23:14.432
And you do not need
to believe that I am real

372
00:23:14.498 --> 00:23:19.237
in order to accept my help
in opening these doors. correct?

373
00:23:36.287 --> 00:23:38.890
All right. All right.

374
00:23:41.125 --> 00:23:43.361
(powering up)

375
00:23:44.262 --> 00:23:47.465
No. no. no. no.
Come on. Come on.

376
00:23:52.003 --> 00:23:54.538
(door whooshes open)

377
00:23:54.605 --> 00:23:56.640
(footsteps approaching)

378
00:23:56.740 --> 00:23:59.743
Spock. you need to see this.

379
00:24:05.083 --> 00:24:07.018
I'm the only one
not affected or...

380
00:24:12.023 --> 00:24:17.361
I can't let what happened here
spread throughout Starfleet.

381
00:24:21.665 --> 00:24:25.436
Whatever happened here. it drove
the Griffin CSO mad. Look.

382
00:24:25.536 --> 00:24:31.009
I can't let what happened here
spread throughout Starfleet.

383
00:24:31.109 --> 00:24:32.944
You know what must be done.

384
00:24:36.780 --> 00:24:38.883
Harper.

385
00:24:38.983 --> 00:24:41.519
What happened to you?

386
00:24:41.619 --> 00:24:45.556
The very same thing that is
happening to you right now.

387
00:24:45.656 --> 00:24:49.627
(powering down and up)

388
00:24:58.002 --> 00:25:00.171
(soft trilling)

389
00:25:01.072 --> 00:25:02.473
Damn it.

390
00:25:03.474 --> 00:25:05.843
(soft mechanical whirring)

391
00:25:27.999 --> 00:25:30.368
(soft mechanical whirring
continues)

392
00:25:35.974 --> 00:25:37.175
(whirring stops)

393
00:25:52.890 --> 00:25:55.059
BABY:
Dada?

394
00:25:58.329 --> 00:26:00.864
(baby cries)

395
00:26:03.667 --> 00:26:05.036
Hello?

396
00:26:09.073 --> 00:26:10.674
Can you hear me?

397
00:26:14.078 --> 00:26:16.614
(baby crying)

398
00:26:31.662 --> 00:26:34.232
(grunts)
No. wait. Wait!

399
00:26:34.332 --> 00:26:36.500
(echoes):
Dada?

400
00:26:37.501 --> 00:26:39.170
David?

401
00:26:40.004 --> 00:26:42.206
Sever the green. then red.

402
00:26:46.244 --> 00:26:48.179
The color scheme of these wires.

403
00:26:48.246 --> 00:26:51.415
Does it look familiar to you?

404
00:26:53.917 --> 00:26:55.786
The holiday spent on Hurk'ah.

405
00:26:55.886 --> 00:26:57.521
T'PRING:
A trip you surprised me with.

406
00:26:57.588 --> 00:26:59.523
Do you also recall what I said

407
00:26:59.590 --> 00:27:01.959
when you told me
of the plans to go?

408
00:27:02.726 --> 00:27:04.895
That you do not care
for surprises.

409
00:27:04.995 --> 00:27:07.098
It was too human an exercise.

410
00:27:07.198 --> 00:27:09.367
I should not have said that.

411
00:27:11.069 --> 00:27:13.137
It was a wonderful trip.

412
00:27:13.937 --> 00:27:15.706
I have sought counseling
to understand

413
00:27:15.806 --> 00:27:18.942
what caused our engagement
to dissolve.

414
00:27:19.043 --> 00:27:21.379
- The reason for that was my...
- My fault.

415
00:27:22.280 --> 00:27:25.649
I did not love you
as you deserved to be loved.

416
00:27:29.953 --> 00:27:32.156
I do not know
what caused you and I

417
00:27:32.256 --> 00:27:34.525
to be in this place
at this time.

418
00:27:34.625 --> 00:27:36.994
But I do know
what it can give us.

419
00:27:41.732 --> 00:27:43.167
A second chance.

420
00:27:54.078 --> 00:27:59.717
HARPER: That itch that's been
gnawing at you for months?

421
00:28:03.487 --> 00:28:05.656
(La'An gasps)

422
00:28:09.593 --> 00:28:13.431
That feeling that something
is wrong with you?

423
00:28:13.531 --> 00:28:16.234
(La'An panting)

424
00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:25.209
La'An Noonien-Singh.

425
00:28:25.343 --> 00:28:27.378
you are not a Khan.

426
00:28:27.478 --> 00:28:29.413
You are not a Romulan.

427
00:28:29.513 --> 00:28:34.051
And you are not a monster.

428
00:28:49.967 --> 00:28:53.036
You're one of us.

429
00:29:06.917 --> 00:29:10.654
I could not see it clearly
until we were parted.

430
00:29:10.721 --> 00:29:14.325
Your humanity
is not your weakness.

431
00:29:14.392 --> 00:29:16.560
It is your biggest strength.

432
00:29:21.165 --> 00:29:23.601
What has held you back
in your relationships

433
00:29:23.734 --> 00:29:26.170
and even your beloved Starfleet

434
00:29:26.237 --> 00:29:28.939
is your Vulcan side.

435
00:29:31.442 --> 00:29:34.512
But here on the Griffin.

436
00:29:34.612 --> 00:29:36.747
we can fix that. Spock.

437
00:29:36.847 --> 00:29:38.115
No. wait.

438
00:29:38.216 --> 00:29:40.418
- We can set you...
- Wait!

439
00:29:41.585 --> 00:29:45.989
- ...free.
- (yelling)

440
00:29:51.229 --> 00:29:54.698
David! David!

441
00:29:55.566 --> 00:29:58.001
(metallic trilling)

442
00:29:58.802 --> 00:30:01.004
(phaser powers up)

443
00:30:10.548 --> 00:30:12.283
(Kirk sighs)

444
00:30:12.350 --> 00:30:14.318
You got Spock's message.

445
00:30:14.452 --> 00:30:18.121
Captain set course
as soon as we received it.

446
00:30:18.188 --> 00:30:19.990
The Griffin.

447
00:30:20.090 --> 00:30:22.993
After all this time.
Kirk. what happened?

448
00:30:23.126 --> 00:30:25.095
I think Jim's had enough
for one day. Ortegas.

449
00:30:25.195 --> 00:30:27.097
We'll investigate after we get
him to Dr. M'Benga.

450
00:30:27.164 --> 00:30:28.399
- Number One?
- (comms chime)

451
00:30:28.499 --> 00:30:29.867
Scotty.
lock onto Kirk's signature

452
00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.902
and transport him
directly to sickbay.

453
00:30:32.002 --> 00:30:33.170
Uh. wait. Captain.

454
00:30:33.271 --> 00:30:35.806
Uh. there's someone else
on board.

455
00:30:35.873 --> 00:30:37.841
a survivor named Harper.

456
00:30:37.941 --> 00:30:39.477
Enterprise. do you copy?

457
00:30:39.543 --> 00:30:41.345
(comms chime)

458
00:30:41.445 --> 00:30:43.814
Uhura. since our communicators
aren't working...

459
00:30:43.914 --> 00:30:45.383
UHURA:
Sir.

460
00:30:45.483 --> 00:30:47.618
this comms station is...

461
00:30:47.685 --> 00:30:50.087
Well...

462
00:30:50.187 --> 00:30:53.223
KIRK:
I had to dig through there.

463
00:30:53.357 --> 00:30:55.459
I'm sorry.

464
00:30:55.526 --> 00:30:58.896
I heard something.

465
00:30:58.996 --> 00:31:00.964
Someone... inside the console.

466
00:31:03.200 --> 00:31:05.903
Was it the survivor? Harper?

467
00:31:06.704 --> 00:31:10.341
I... I heard David.

468
00:31:11.375 --> 00:31:13.143
Your son?

469
00:31:15.979 --> 00:31:19.216
Jim. he's on his way
to Epsilon-5.

470
00:31:19.983 --> 00:31:22.520
Carol waited
as long as she could.

471
00:31:23.253 --> 00:31:26.524
But in her defense. you did say
you'd be home three days ago.

472
00:31:29.927 --> 00:31:31.395
Sir. we have
to get off this ship

473
00:31:31.529 --> 00:31:33.597
before whatever's affecting me
affects you all.

474
00:31:33.731 --> 00:31:35.499
All right. everybody. how
do we get back to Enterprise?

475
00:31:35.566 --> 00:31:36.634
Best idea wins. Go.

476
00:31:36.734 --> 00:31:38.402
Spacewalk? Tethered to the ship?

477
00:31:38.536 --> 00:31:40.404
UNA: Fun. but EV suits on the
Griffin are unaccounted for.

478
00:31:40.504 --> 00:31:41.739
(baby crying)

479
00:31:41.872 --> 00:31:44.342
UHURA: Telemetry array
is still operational.

480
00:31:44.442 --> 00:31:47.511
(fading): Gets us in the ballpark
for a transporter signal.

481
00:31:47.611 --> 00:31:49.780
(baby crying)

482
00:31:55.152 --> 00:31:57.988
(baby cries continue)

483
00:32:03.093 --> 00:32:04.795
Jim?

484
00:32:04.928 --> 00:32:06.764
Hey. maybe you should
have a seat. huh?

485
00:32:06.864 --> 00:32:08.231
Come on.

486
00:32:09.833 --> 00:32:11.902
They're going
to find La'An and Spock.

487
00:32:12.002 --> 00:32:16.273
Uhura thinks that she can
transport us off one at a time.

488
00:32:16.374 --> 00:32:18.241
Take a minute.

489
00:32:18.308 --> 00:32:20.911
When your head is clear...

490
00:32:20.978 --> 00:32:22.846
get to the transporter.

491
00:32:24.247 --> 00:32:25.449
(sighs)

492
00:32:26.850 --> 00:32:28.486
Sam.

493
00:32:30.388 --> 00:32:32.490
I don't know
what's wrong with me.

494
00:32:37.294 --> 00:32:39.430
I don't know either.

495
00:32:39.530 --> 00:32:42.032
But you're gonna be okay.

496
00:32:43.634 --> 00:32:45.836
(panting)

497
00:32:54.612 --> 00:32:56.113
Bridge.

498
00:32:57.581 --> 00:32:58.849
(sighs)

499
00:32:58.949 --> 00:33:01.685
(turbolift whirring)

500
00:33:01.819 --> 00:33:04.722
- (chime)
- COMPUTER: Deck 17.

501
00:33:07.858 --> 00:33:10.528
Let's try that again. shall we?

502
00:33:10.628 --> 00:33:12.796
Bridge.

503
00:33:14.632 --> 00:33:17.134
(turbolift whirring)

504
00:33:19.369 --> 00:33:22.706
- (chime)
- Deck 17.

505
00:33:25.208 --> 00:33:27.010
Computer. bridge.

506
00:33:27.110 --> 00:33:28.879
(door closes)

507
00:33:29.012 --> 00:33:31.214
(turbolift whirring)

508
00:33:32.115 --> 00:33:34.685
(sighs)

509
00:33:38.656 --> 00:33:41.692
- (chime)
- Deck 17...

510
00:33:41.792 --> 00:33:43.994
La'An.

511
00:33:44.094 --> 00:33:46.930
(lights softly clicking)

512
00:33:54.204 --> 00:33:56.406
(sighs)

513
00:34:02.345 --> 00:34:04.548
(rhythmic creaking)

514
00:34:28.872 --> 00:34:31.108
(rhythmic creaking continues)

515
00:34:45.956 --> 00:34:48.759
(panting softly)

516
00:35:03.941 --> 00:35:05.609
(thud)

517
00:35:07.310 --> 00:35:09.279
HARPER:
It's all my fault.

518
00:35:09.379 --> 00:35:11.815
- (blows landing)
- (Harper yells)

519
00:35:27.898 --> 00:35:31.001
It was my job
to keep the crew safe.

520
00:35:42.079 --> 00:35:44.514
And I failed.

521
00:35:44.648 --> 00:35:47.217
But it's not too late for you.

522
00:35:51.488 --> 00:35:53.156
(yells)

523
00:35:53.256 --> 00:35:55.859
(panting)

524
00:36:04.501 --> 00:36:05.969
- UHURA: La'An?
- (footsteps approaching)

525
00:36:06.069 --> 00:36:07.337
La'An. hey.

526
00:36:07.470 --> 00:36:09.006
Come here. Oh.

527
00:36:09.106 --> 00:36:10.473
Oh.

528
00:36:11.274 --> 00:36:14.645
Whatever happened here must be
really bad if you're hugging.

529
00:36:14.745 --> 00:36:16.313
Let's get the hell out of here.

530
00:36:16.379 --> 00:36:19.583
Yeah. There's our girl.
Come on.

531
00:36:23.386 --> 00:36:24.888
Friend of yours?

532
00:36:25.022 --> 00:36:27.090
Not in the slightest.

533
00:36:31.394 --> 00:36:33.030
T'PRING:
Our love died

534
00:36:33.130 --> 00:36:35.465
because your heart

535
00:36:35.532 --> 00:36:39.770
was not in the right place.

536
00:36:44.374 --> 00:36:46.543
Let's change that. shall we?

537
00:36:46.644 --> 00:36:48.946
(panting)

538
00:36:50.013 --> 00:36:51.615
No.

539
00:36:51.715 --> 00:36:53.450
No. stop.

540
00:36:54.551 --> 00:36:55.986
PIKE (distant):
Spock. is that you?

541
00:36:56.086 --> 00:36:57.587
Captain! Help!

542
00:36:59.389 --> 00:37:00.991
UNA:
Easy. We've got you.

543
00:37:01.058 --> 00:37:03.460
You're safe now. you understand?

544
00:37:04.261 --> 00:37:06.229
T'Pring. she tied me down.

545
00:37:06.329 --> 00:37:07.698
T'Pring?

546
00:37:07.798 --> 00:37:09.833
As in your ex T'Pring?

547
00:37:09.933 --> 00:37:11.935
She is dangerous.

548
00:37:12.035 --> 00:37:14.805
You know. I never liked her.

549
00:37:14.905 --> 00:37:16.606
(grunts)

550
00:37:16.707 --> 00:37:18.308
KIRK:
All right.

551
00:37:19.242 --> 00:37:22.245
- Let's roll.
- All right.

552
00:37:22.345 --> 00:37:24.948
Oh. Who's this little guy?

553
00:37:25.883 --> 00:37:28.185
- (sighs)
- Reminds me of the tchotchkes

554
00:37:28.285 --> 00:37:31.288
Dad used to bring home
when he was home on leave.

555
00:37:31.388 --> 00:37:33.423
Like some kind of.
I don't know...

556
00:37:33.523 --> 00:37:36.026
Apology for not being around.

557
00:37:36.126 --> 00:37:37.761
I have more of these
crappy little things

558
00:37:37.861 --> 00:37:41.431
in a box somewhere than I have
memories of playing with Dad.

559
00:37:41.531 --> 00:37:43.066
(laughs softly)

560
00:37:43.133 --> 00:37:46.003
I mean. when was the last time
you even heard from the old man?

561
00:37:46.937 --> 00:37:49.606
- Birthday.
- Birthday. Right.

562
00:37:49.707 --> 00:37:51.742
How do you do it. Sam?

563
00:37:52.475 --> 00:37:56.279
How do you balance
Starfleet and family?

564
00:37:57.280 --> 00:37:58.682
Well. I...

565
00:37:59.549 --> 00:38:00.984
I don't.

566
00:38:01.719 --> 00:38:04.054
But I get home
as often as I can.

567
00:38:04.154 --> 00:38:06.089
And every night I call my boys.

568
00:38:06.189 --> 00:38:08.759
sign off with the same thing.

569
00:38:09.526 --> 00:38:10.961
"Good night. I love you.

570
00:38:11.061 --> 00:38:13.130
and I'll see you
in your dreams."

571
00:38:15.799 --> 00:38:18.635
We get out of here
safe and sound.

572
00:38:18.736 --> 00:38:21.104
I'm gonna do that for David.

573
00:38:21.939 --> 00:38:24.107
So let's get out of here. then.

574
00:38:24.174 --> 00:38:25.909
BOY (distant):
Dad.

575
00:38:25.976 --> 00:38:27.377
Wait.

576
00:38:28.178 --> 00:38:29.646
Wait. do you hear that?

577
00:38:29.747 --> 00:38:32.249
- Dad.
- Is that... is that Peter?

578
00:38:32.315 --> 00:38:34.584
Whoa. whoa. Hey. hey. hey. Sam.
It's not real.

579
00:38:34.651 --> 00:38:37.320
- It's not real.
- No. no. That's my little boy. That's my boy.

580
00:38:37.420 --> 00:38:39.289
Sam. Sam. listen to me.

581
00:38:39.356 --> 00:38:41.825
It's not real.

582
00:38:41.959 --> 00:38:42.960
Okay.

583
00:38:43.060 --> 00:38:44.561
We have to get out of here now.

584
00:38:44.661 --> 00:38:46.764
- Come on. Let's go.
- Okay.

585
00:38:50.167 --> 00:38:53.436
(door beeping)

586
00:38:53.503 --> 00:38:56.006
Ready room. We can get out...

587
00:39:00.377 --> 00:39:01.845
UHURA:
Okay. we're set.

588
00:39:01.979 --> 00:39:04.214
But I was right. We can
only transport one at a time.

589
00:39:04.347 --> 00:39:06.149
LA'AN: We have to get you two
out of here first

590
00:39:06.216 --> 00:39:07.417
before Harper finds us

591
00:39:07.517 --> 00:39:09.219
or this ship affects you
as it has me.

592
00:39:09.352 --> 00:39:12.055
- No arguments. You understand?
- Who's arguing?

593
00:39:13.456 --> 00:39:15.292
Get me off this dump.

594
00:39:19.863 --> 00:39:22.099
Wait. No.

595
00:39:22.199 --> 00:39:23.566
Something's wrong.

596
00:39:23.700 --> 00:39:25.368
(grunting)

597
00:39:26.236 --> 00:39:28.271
(screaming)

598
00:39:30.707 --> 00:39:32.109
Let me...

599
00:39:33.143 --> 00:39:35.678
- What did you do?
- What? No. I...

600
00:39:37.848 --> 00:39:39.482
- I...
- Erica! Hang on.

601
00:39:39.549 --> 00:39:41.318
I'm transporting you
into the buffer.

602
00:39:41.418 --> 00:39:43.620
(screaming continues)

603
00:39:53.330 --> 00:39:56.699
You set the transporter
to beam Erica into herself.

604
00:39:56.800 --> 00:39:57.935
To fuse her.

605
00:39:58.035 --> 00:39:59.402
Nyota. let me explain.
Please. I...

606
00:39:59.502 --> 00:40:01.004
- No. No.
- Nyota.

607
00:40:01.071 --> 00:40:03.606
- (panting): Oh. my God.
- Nyota.

608
00:40:05.442 --> 00:40:07.244
Clearly.
something is manipulating

609
00:40:07.344 --> 00:40:09.046
whoever boards the Griffin.

610
00:40:09.112 --> 00:40:11.181
We must get you both
off this malignant ship.

611
00:40:11.281 --> 00:40:12.615
Easy. easy. easy.

612
00:40:12.749 --> 00:40:14.484
What did Pike tell you?

613
00:40:20.891 --> 00:40:23.360
You're safe now. Spock.

614
00:40:23.460 --> 00:40:25.028
SPOCK:
No.

615
00:40:26.396 --> 00:40:28.431
PIKE: You just need to listen
to the ship.

616
00:40:28.565 --> 00:40:30.033
I mean...

617
00:40:30.100 --> 00:40:32.202
can't you hear it?

618
00:40:33.070 --> 00:40:35.105
All it wants to do
is set us free.

619
00:40:35.205 --> 00:40:36.606
(tightens strap)

620
00:40:36.706 --> 00:40:38.775
Una. with your enhanced Illyrian
blood. you should be able

621
00:40:38.876 --> 00:40:40.077
- to fight off...
- My blood

622
00:40:40.177 --> 00:40:42.045
is what's been
holding me back. Spock.

623
00:40:42.112 --> 00:40:43.546
Starfleet will never
promote me to captain

624
00:40:43.613 --> 00:40:45.382
as long as I'm an Illyrian.

625
00:40:45.482 --> 00:40:47.184
But here...

626
00:40:47.284 --> 00:40:49.552
(whispers):
I can be free of that.

627
00:40:49.619 --> 00:40:51.855
Una. please do not!

628
00:40:58.996 --> 00:41:00.163
(sighs happily)

629
00:41:00.263 --> 00:41:01.364
(body thuds)

630
00:41:01.464 --> 00:41:03.633
(panting)

631
00:41:06.836 --> 00:41:09.706
- (grunting)
- (metal creaking)

632
00:41:14.277 --> 00:41:16.479
(both panting)

633
00:41:21.151 --> 00:41:22.419
(sighs)

634
00:41:22.485 --> 00:41:26.389
We're never getting
off this ship. are we?

635
00:41:34.697 --> 00:41:37.034
We're gonna die.

636
00:41:37.901 --> 00:41:39.937
Out here...

637
00:41:40.003 --> 00:41:41.871
in space.

638
00:41:43.006 --> 00:41:44.841
Alone.

639
00:41:45.875 --> 00:41:48.145
Like Kirks are born to do.

640
00:41:48.245 --> 00:41:50.380
- Sam. listen to me.
- (glass cracking)

641
00:41:58.321 --> 00:41:59.389
Sam?

642
00:41:59.522 --> 00:42:01.224
Help me with the door.

643
00:42:01.358 --> 00:42:02.692
Sam!

644
00:42:02.792 --> 00:42:03.860
(grunts)

645
00:42:03.961 --> 00:42:05.062
Sam!

646
00:42:05.195 --> 00:42:08.365
Sam. it's gonna break.
It's gonna break!

647
00:42:08.498 --> 00:42:10.533
Get away from it.

648
00:42:12.602 --> 00:42:14.504
My brother.

649
00:42:14.604 --> 00:42:16.839
Always the hero.

650
00:42:17.540 --> 00:42:19.342
But you can't save everyone.

651
00:42:20.110 --> 00:42:23.080
You have to make peace
with that. Jim.

652
00:42:24.081 --> 00:42:26.549
Sam. it's the ship.
Don't listen to it.

653
00:42:26.683 --> 00:42:28.551
- Until you accept that...
- Don't listen to it.

654
00:42:28.651 --> 00:42:32.055
...you will never be free.

655
00:42:32.189 --> 00:42:33.656
But don't worry.

656
00:42:33.756 --> 00:42:35.758
The Griffin's gonna
show you the way.

657
00:42:35.892 --> 00:42:37.260
(heavy thud)

658
00:42:40.863 --> 00:42:43.166
- No!
- (screams)

659
00:42:43.266 --> 00:42:44.667
No!

660
00:42:44.734 --> 00:42:47.270
Sam. Sam.

661
00:42:47.370 --> 00:42:50.140
(grunting)

662
00:42:52.675 --> 00:42:54.077
Jim.

663
00:42:54.877 --> 00:42:56.913
Tell my babies good night.

664
00:42:57.047 --> 00:42:59.849
That I love them.

665
00:42:59.916 --> 00:43:01.751
And I'll see them in their...

666
00:43:03.053 --> 00:43:04.454
No!

667
00:43:06.589 --> 00:43:08.491
No!

668
00:43:15.898 --> 00:43:17.900
Nyota. listen to me. please.

669
00:43:18.001 --> 00:43:20.837
I need to get you off this ship.

670
00:43:21.704 --> 00:43:23.006
(strains)

671
00:43:23.906 --> 00:43:24.907
Nyota.

672
00:43:24.974 --> 00:43:26.543
Look at yourself. La'An.

673
00:43:26.643 --> 00:43:28.378
Something isn't right.

674
00:43:28.445 --> 00:43:29.679
No.
(sighs)

675
00:43:29.779 --> 00:43:32.315
Something is definitely
not right.

676
00:43:32.415 --> 00:43:34.417
But Ortegas is alive
and safe in the buffer.

677
00:43:34.517 --> 00:43:36.886
and I need your help
to get us back to Enterprise

678
00:43:36.953 --> 00:43:38.455
so we can save her.

679
00:43:39.789 --> 00:43:40.923
(exhales)

680
00:43:40.990 --> 00:43:42.525
Please. Nyota.

681
00:43:44.094 --> 00:43:46.163
What is wrong with this place?

682
00:43:46.963 --> 00:43:48.131
Look out.

683
00:43:48.231 --> 00:43:49.199
(grunts)

684
00:43:49.299 --> 00:43:51.468
(panting)

685
00:43:58.408 --> 00:43:59.942
It's time to let go. La'An.

686
00:44:00.009 --> 00:44:04.081
On the Griffin. you can
finally be your true self.

687
00:44:05.582 --> 00:44:07.484
I mean...

688
00:44:09.086 --> 00:44:11.821
...look what you've
accomplished here already.

689
00:44:14.624 --> 00:44:16.826
Please don't
kill me. La'An. Please.

690
00:44:16.959 --> 00:44:19.196
Please. please.

691
00:44:19.329 --> 00:44:21.364
Please don't kill me.

692
00:44:26.503 --> 00:44:28.205
(exhales)

693
00:44:28.305 --> 00:44:30.039
(whimpers)

694
00:44:30.140 --> 00:44:31.541
(receding footsteps)

695
00:44:34.477 --> 00:44:36.413
(sighing)

696
00:44:47.524 --> 00:44:49.292
Welcome home.

697
00:44:59.136 --> 00:45:00.503
KIRK:
La'An.

698
00:45:00.603 --> 00:45:02.639
(door whooshes shut)

699
00:45:02.705 --> 00:45:04.374
(panting):
Thank God you're okay.

700
00:45:04.507 --> 00:45:07.110
Listen to me. we have to get
to the transporter.

701
00:45:07.210 --> 00:45:09.379
(baby crying)

702
00:45:12.649 --> 00:45:13.816
Tell me you don't hear that.

703
00:45:13.883 --> 00:45:16.819
- (grunts)
- (exhales)

704
00:45:17.687 --> 00:45:19.556
(gasping)

705
00:45:19.656 --> 00:45:22.359
(whispers):
I hear everything now.

706
00:45:27.864 --> 00:45:30.032
♪ ♪

707
00:45:34.871 --> 00:45:36.739
This ship is amazing. Spock.

708
00:45:37.540 --> 00:45:40.810
I mean.
all the freshest ingredients.

709
00:45:40.910 --> 00:45:42.245
(laughs)

710
00:45:43.680 --> 00:45:46.249
If I stay on board
the Griffin...

711
00:45:47.884 --> 00:45:50.187
...I can be free of my fate.

712
00:45:50.253 --> 00:45:52.054
I don't have to be
the captain anymore.

713
00:45:54.791 --> 00:45:57.494
I can be the head chef.

714
00:45:58.828 --> 00:46:01.231
- (giggles)
- (chopping)

715
00:46:03.400 --> 00:46:05.602
(grunting)

716
00:46:10.407 --> 00:46:12.275
(gasps)

717
00:46:15.745 --> 00:46:18.915
Whatever you are. please...

718
00:46:19.716 --> 00:46:21.318
...let them go.

719
00:46:22.118 --> 00:46:24.254
Let them go and take me.

720
00:46:24.354 --> 00:46:27.023
Ever so noble.

721
00:46:27.890 --> 00:46:30.493
Ever so logical.

722
00:46:31.428 --> 00:46:34.264
But logic has no place here.

723
00:46:36.366 --> 00:46:41.271
And yet that is what you have
inadvertently brought to me.

724
00:46:45.107 --> 00:46:47.410
(reciting poem in Vulcan)

725
00:46:47.510 --> 00:46:49.011
What are you doing?

726
00:46:51.180 --> 00:46:53.783
"It will guide you home."

727
00:46:58.355 --> 00:47:01.157
(continues reciting in Vulcan)

728
00:47:03.560 --> 00:47:05.828
(reciting louder)

729
00:47:16.506 --> 00:47:18.708
(electricity buzzing)

730
00:47:44.334 --> 00:47:46.636
- (footsteps)
- (Kirk grunting)

731
00:47:51.374 --> 00:47:52.509
LA'AN:
The ship picked Harper.

732
00:47:52.642 --> 00:47:55.011
and now it's picked us.

733
00:47:55.111 --> 00:47:57.647
The Griffin needs
a captain. James.

734
00:47:57.747 --> 00:47:59.015
And who better to captain

735
00:47:59.115 --> 00:48:01.050
a ship of the damned
than a Kirk?

736
00:48:01.183 --> 00:48:03.019
(panting):
This isn't you.

737
00:48:03.152 --> 00:48:05.054
This isn't you.

738
00:48:05.187 --> 00:48:06.889
This is me.

739
00:48:08.257 --> 00:48:09.392
The real me.

740
00:48:09.492 --> 00:48:11.861
(straining)

741
00:48:11.961 --> 00:48:16.933
And you can feel this way. too.
if you just let go.

742
00:48:18.435 --> 00:48:21.037
Why won't you let go?

743
00:48:21.170 --> 00:48:23.306
(panting)

744
00:48:24.741 --> 00:48:26.709
David.

745
00:48:27.644 --> 00:48:30.146
(laughs)

746
00:48:40.390 --> 00:48:42.091
Your little boy

747
00:48:42.224 --> 00:48:45.428
is going to die just like you.

748
00:48:45.562 --> 00:48:48.197
At the end of a blade.

749
00:48:48.264 --> 00:48:52.435
Bleeding out
in a dark corner of space.

750
00:49:11.921 --> 00:49:13.423
KIRK:
It's okay.

751
00:49:14.223 --> 00:49:17.293
You're okay. You're okay.

752
00:49:28.405 --> 00:49:31.408
(crying)

753
00:49:36.613 --> 00:49:38.114
- My...
- Jim.

754
00:49:38.214 --> 00:49:39.882
- My...
- Oh.

755
00:49:39.982 --> 00:49:42.485
My b... my brother Sam.

756
00:49:43.285 --> 00:49:44.887
Is he. is he okay?

757
00:49:44.987 --> 00:49:46.589
Your brother?

758
00:49:46.689 --> 00:49:48.625
He's on shore leave
visiting his family.

759
00:49:48.725 --> 00:49:50.493
Jim.

760
00:49:51.293 --> 00:49:52.962
Jim. Jim.

761
00:50:09.979 --> 00:50:12.482
M'BENGA: So. what will become
of the Griffin?

762
00:50:12.582 --> 00:50:13.816
Well. the USS Thorn has arrived

763
00:50:13.950 --> 00:50:15.418
to tow the ship
back to wherever the hell

764
00:50:15.518 --> 00:50:18.688
Division 12's base of operations
is located.

765
00:50:19.522 --> 00:50:21.090
How many cases
have you referred to them

766
00:50:21.190 --> 00:50:22.859
in your career. Chris?

767
00:50:22.992 --> 00:50:24.427
Six.

768
00:50:24.494 --> 00:50:26.095
Four were resolved
with scientific

769
00:50:26.195 --> 00:50:27.930
or alien explanations.

770
00:50:28.798 --> 00:50:30.232
And the other two?

771
00:50:32.001 --> 00:50:34.070
I'll let you know
when I find out.

772
00:50:34.871 --> 00:50:36.238
So. how's Jim?

773
00:50:37.006 --> 00:50:38.641
M'BENGA:
He's healing well.

774
00:50:38.708 --> 00:50:40.443
But he was truly convinced
that you and the boarding party

775
00:50:40.510 --> 00:50:43.112
actually beamed
onto the Griffin.

776
00:50:43.179 --> 00:50:45.381
PIKE:
And Spock and La'An?

777
00:50:50.319 --> 00:50:53.122
Physically. they're all fine.

778
00:50:53.189 --> 00:50:54.591
Mentally?

779
00:51:04.133 --> 00:51:05.334
CHAPEL:
Good as new.

780
00:51:05.401 --> 00:51:08.705
And just as pointy
as I remember.

781
00:51:11.207 --> 00:51:12.942
(sighs)
How do they feel?

782
00:51:17.547 --> 00:51:19.148
They feel like me.

783
00:51:19.916 --> 00:51:22.719
I'll pass your compliments
on to the chef.

784
00:51:25.387 --> 00:51:27.423
Thank you for coming
to my quarters. Christine.

785
00:51:27.524 --> 00:51:29.191
I recognize
the request was illogical.

786
00:51:29.291 --> 00:51:30.693
but after what transpired
on the Griffin...

787
00:51:30.760 --> 00:51:33.329
Sickbay was the last place
you wanted to be?

788
00:51:33.429 --> 00:51:36.866
I hate eating in the mess hall
for the same reason.

789
00:51:36.933 --> 00:51:39.869
During the war.
I was briefly stationed

790
00:51:39.969 --> 00:51:42.371
at the hospital on Yrti.

791
00:51:42.471 --> 00:51:44.073
I am sorry to hear that.

792
00:51:44.173 --> 00:51:46.008
The Yrti offensive
took heavy casualties.

793
00:51:46.075 --> 00:51:49.211
When the OR got blasted.
we had to triage

794
00:51:49.311 --> 00:51:51.681
and operate in the mess.

795
00:51:52.849 --> 00:51:55.251
Wasn't the most appetizing place
to begin with.

796
00:51:55.384 --> 00:51:59.055
but... after that night...

797
00:52:04.527 --> 00:52:06.162
Are you okay?

798
00:52:10.767 --> 00:52:12.835
I am fine. Christine.

799
00:52:18.975 --> 00:52:22.378
Thank you for making
this "house call."

800
00:52:22.444 --> 00:52:23.846
Of course.

801
00:52:30.286 --> 00:52:32.488
Can I ask one question?

802
00:52:34.724 --> 00:52:36.458
Why T'Pring?

803
00:52:36.593 --> 00:52:38.961
I believe whatever probed
my mind selected her

804
00:52:39.061 --> 00:52:42.565
to extract the most
emotional response it could.

805
00:52:42.665 --> 00:52:45.301
But the illusion was powered
by my own memories.

806
00:52:45.401 --> 00:52:47.169
My own beliefs.

807
00:52:48.004 --> 00:52:50.673
That anchored me.
Brought me back.

808
00:52:50.773 --> 00:52:52.742
To her?

809
00:52:54.744 --> 00:52:56.312
To logic.

810
00:53:00.516 --> 00:53:02.451
I don't understand.
What's the problem?

811
00:53:02.551 --> 00:53:05.321
The problem. sir.
is that your report

812
00:53:05.454 --> 00:53:09.759
on the Griffin incident is.
is missing some key data.

813
00:53:09.826 --> 00:53:11.360
Like what?

814
00:53:12.128 --> 00:53:15.665
Like the fact that I tried
to kill James Kirk?

815
00:53:17.199 --> 00:53:19.301
Have you talked to him?
Or Spock?

816
00:53:20.937 --> 00:53:22.304
No.

817
00:53:23.139 --> 00:53:24.974
Okay.

818
00:53:25.074 --> 00:53:26.375
Have a seat and have a drink.

819
00:53:26.475 --> 00:53:29.746
Don't make me
make that an order.

820
00:53:48.030 --> 00:53:50.366
James saw his son.

821
00:53:50.499 --> 00:53:51.834
Spock his ex.

822
00:53:51.901 --> 00:53:53.703
And you're wondering
why you saw Harper.

823
00:53:53.803 --> 00:53:56.405
No. I know why.

824
00:53:57.640 --> 00:53:59.408
Starfleet is my family.

825
00:54:00.176 --> 00:54:03.579
I just want to know
what happened to the crew.

826
00:54:03.713 --> 00:54:05.915
To Harper.

827
00:54:07.283 --> 00:54:09.952
Ever tell you about
my Uncle Art's farm?

828
00:54:11.587 --> 00:54:13.455
- Sir?
- It's a beautiful thing.

829
00:54:13.555 --> 00:54:14.590
35 acres.

830
00:54:14.724 --> 00:54:17.493
And it had this old creaky barn

831
00:54:17.559 --> 00:54:19.929
that my cousins swore
was haunted

832
00:54:20.062 --> 00:54:22.598
by a woman carrying a scythe.

833
00:54:23.365 --> 00:54:27.704
And I slept out in that barn
to prove it was all nonsense.

834
00:54:27.804 --> 00:54:29.471
And I was right.

835
00:54:30.873 --> 00:54:32.441
Till I wasn't.

836
00:54:33.242 --> 00:54:35.511
Just before I drifted off...

837
00:54:36.612 --> 00:54:40.249
...I heard steel

838
00:54:40.349 --> 00:54:43.185
scraping across the floor

839
00:54:43.252 --> 00:54:47.089
and a-a voice that whispered.

840
00:54:47.189 --> 00:54:50.359
(whispers):
"I know your true name."

841
00:54:50.426 --> 00:54:52.661
I ran out of there
about as fast as I could.

842
00:54:52.762 --> 00:54:54.997
Cut my arm on a nail
on the way out.

843
00:54:55.097 --> 00:54:57.266
Now. come sunrise.
my family searched that barn

844
00:54:57.366 --> 00:55:00.803
top to bottom.
didn't find a damn thing.

845
00:55:02.104 --> 00:55:04.006
But I still have that scar.

846
00:55:04.106 --> 00:55:06.642
Space is limitless in its beauty

847
00:55:06.743 --> 00:55:08.577
and in its terror.

848
00:55:09.912 --> 00:55:12.081
Whatever you encountered.

849
00:55:12.181 --> 00:55:16.352
the only thing that matters
is that you survived.

850
00:55:21.623 --> 00:55:25.394
And that is all Starfleet
needs to know.

851
00:55:28.630 --> 00:55:30.199
Case closed.

852
00:55:38.474 --> 00:55:40.309
Carol and David
are pretty far out.

853
00:55:40.442 --> 00:55:44.346
so I relayed a signal
off a starbase or two.

854
00:55:44.480 --> 00:55:47.984
Press this button
and you will hail her outpost.

855
00:55:50.319 --> 00:55:51.687
Got it.

856
00:55:52.889 --> 00:55:54.857
And the cookies?

857
00:55:55.657 --> 00:55:56.826
(laughs softly)

858
00:55:56.926 --> 00:55:59.028
Someone once told me
that refusing

859
00:55:59.161 --> 00:56:01.998
freshly made cookies
is a clear sign of madness.

860
00:56:02.098 --> 00:56:03.766
Mm.

861
00:56:04.600 --> 00:56:08.170
You're worried that I lost
my mind on the Griffin?

862
00:56:08.270 --> 00:56:11.073
If you don't want the cookies.
I'll just...

863
00:56:15.344 --> 00:56:17.046
Are you all right?

864
00:56:20.983 --> 00:56:22.751
(sighs)

865
00:56:24.887 --> 00:56:26.923
Yes.

866
00:56:28.891 --> 00:56:31.360
You're gonna be okay. Jim.

867
00:56:35.131 --> 00:56:37.133
How do you know?

868
00:56:41.137 --> 00:56:42.404
Nyota.

869
00:56:45.341 --> 00:56:47.476
Thank you.

870
00:56:48.377 --> 00:56:50.880
Always happy to be of service.

871
00:57:08.730 --> 00:57:10.933
(connection ringing)

872
00:57:24.847 --> 00:57:26.815
(sighs)

873
00:57:34.490 --> 00:57:36.492
(shudders)

874
